    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d112-a5">

                <pb facs="0499" n="285" xml:id="pg285"/>

                <head>Mr. Washburne to Mr. Moran</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1871-01-01"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 1, 1871.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Moran:</hi> Please send me no more London
                    papers; only cut out the telegraphic dispatches from the United States, from day
                    to day, and send them. It is too much to be the only person, in a city of two
                    millions of people, who receives any outside news. It has become a great
                    annoyance, and I prefer being without news to being subject to it. I hope you
                    will receive permission to send all my private letters. I expect you will send
                    me all the American papers as usual.</p>
                <p>Yours, truly,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E. B. WASHBURNE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
